# Duet-512 NEON

Status: retained for Duet-512 v2 on ARM NEON.

The 3-column permutation stores two columns in one `uint64x2_t` and keeps the
third column in a scalar lane. The final `l64` rotate/xor layer now uses scalar
`ROR` per packed lane instead of NEON variable-shift rotate emulation. This v2
version is KAT-clean and faster than the pure-C v2 path on the local ARM
machine.

See `../Evaluation_Report.md` for validation commands and benchmark results.
